{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 25, :comments ["<b>And he removed the wheel of his chariots.</b> By way of the plain sense (peshat): since the pillar of fire, which burned every piece of wood in their implements of war, and the pillar of cloud, which moistened the ground, gazed upon them, the chariots were slipping and their strength was completely removed." "<b>And by way of</b> reason (sekhel): אופן is a term for a wheel, as is said (Ezekiel 10:13) ״ואופנים להם״ — its meaning is wheels; and likewise (ibid. 1:15) ״והנה אופן אחד בארץ״, which Targum Yonatan renders גלגלא. And Scripture says that the wheel — that is, the source of the power of His chariots — He removed from its might and strength. And since He removed the wheel of His chariots above, He drove him with heaviness below. And so our Rabbis, of blessed memory, interpreted: no nation falls until its prince falls first. And this wheel is the sphere of Mars, by which the Egyptians were worthy of victory and dominance, were it not for HaShem who was for us and fought for Israel. And the power of that sphere is Samael, and the word אפ״ן is deficient in its ו, equal to its numerical value, and behold you have the name of the power and the sphere alluded to in the verse. And this is not to say that the star was the prince of Egypt, for the prince of Egypt was Uzza, and Scripture mentioned him by the name מצרים above: ״והנה מצרים נוסע אחריהם״, for the power attached to a nation is called by the name of the nation, in the language of (Genesis 12:6) ״והכנעני אז בארץ״, as I explained there."], :book :exodus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 14, :notes {1 "The text says אופן (defective, = 141); the comment notes that אפ״ן written without ו equals the numerical value of סמא״ל (also 131). The phrase 'כחשבונו' is translated literally; the gematria is presented exactly as he writes it without verifying or correcting."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:59:10.368762387Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}